{"id":"onboarding-help-new","title":"Get help when blocked","summary":"Have a reachable initial contact and a fallback when the usual route fails","bootstrap":true,"timing":"anytime","escalation":["$general_contacts"],"body":"General support: $general_contacts\n\nBefore company access, use this explicitly supplied route: $preaccess_route\nIf it is unavailable, use the fallback: $fallback_route\n\nDescribe the activity, the nonsecret error and what you already tried.\nNever send passwords, recovery codes, tokens or a complete private record.\nA request being sent is not proof of access. Tell the owner when a blocker\nprevents later work so support can be rearranged without blaming the date.","variables":[{"name":"general_contacts","description":"Who can help with an onboarding problem?","type":"contact","multiple":true,"required":true,"audience":"onboarder"},{"name":"preaccess_route","description":"Which approved business route can the newcomer use before company access?","type":"string","required":true,"audience":"onboarder"},{"name":"fallback_route","description":"What should the newcomer do if the initial route or usual contact is unavailable?","type":"string","required":true,"audience":"onboarder"}],"steps":[{"id":"locate-support","name":"Locate the initial and fallback help routes","checks":[{"ask":"Can you identify a route available before company access and a fallback if it fails?"}]}]}
